      plan: [{ en: 'Common: no change in company value.', zh: '共通：公司價值不變。' }, { en: 'Differences: direction, ratio, price effect, purpose.', zh: '分別：方向、比例、價錢影響、目的。' }, { en: 'Custodian: adjust units and price, fractional rights, block, inform, reconcile.', zh: '託管人：調單位同價、碎股權、凍結、通知、對賬。' }],
      points: [
        { en: 'Neither changes the balance sheet or company value', zh: '兩者都唔改變公司價值', kw: ['value', 'not change|unchanged|does not change|neither|no change|without changing'] },
        { en: 'Split: more shares, lower price (e.g. 1:5)', zh: '拆股：多股、低價', kw: ['split', 'lower|decrease|falls'] },
        { en: 'Reverse split: fewer shares, higher price (e.g. 4:1)', zh: '合股：少股、高價', kw: ['reverse', 'higher|increase|rises'] },
        { en: 'Purpose: split makes shares affordable; reverse makes cheap shares look expensive', zh: '目的', kw: ['affordable|attract|investor'] },
        { en: 'Fractional new shares → tradeable rights', zh: '碎股 → 可買賣權', kw: ['fraction'] },
        { en: 'Custodian blocks, adjusts units and price, informs customers, reconciles', zh: '託管人凍結、調整、通知、對賬', kw: ['block|adjust'] },
      ],
      model: 'Both a share split and a reverse split exchange old shares for new shares at a fixed ratio, and neither of them changes the balance sheet or the value of the company. In a share split, for example at 1:5, each old share becomes five new shares, so the price falls by the same ratio. This makes expensive shares affordable for more investors. In contrast, a reverse split, for example at 4:1, combines several old shares into one new share, so the price rises by the same ratio. It is used to make shares with a very small value look more attractive, and tradeable rights are issued for fractional new shares. In both cases, the custodian must adjust the number of units and the price in every customer depot on the effective date, inform the customers, and block the security until the adjustment is complete. Afterwards it should reconcile with the depository, because the DWP Bank case shows that adjusting the price without the units can cause a huge loss.',
      modelZh: '兩者都按比例換股，唔改變公司價值。拆股（1:5）股數多、價錢低，令人買得起；合股（4:1）股數少、價錢高，令平股睇落吸引，碎股發權。託管人要調整單位同價錢、通知客戶、調整期間凍結，之後對賬——DWP 案例就係只調價唔調單位。',
      phrases: ['Both ... and ... exchange old shares for new shares at a fixed ratio.', 'In contrast, a reverse split ...', 'In both cases, the custodian must ...', 'The DWP Bank case shows that ...'],
